# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution; 1 rad = 1.59 mm). hv0.sim_dist, zeroed at the failure, is how
# far the axis went.
# The F4 stops at speed (the F3 brakes), then comes back: once LinuxCNC
# toggles enable (the drive went to a fault meanwhile, hv timeout), the
# axis moves again.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_f4_dead = 1
run 0.3
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_f3_brake
hv0.sim_f4_dead = 0
lcnc 0 0
run 0.1
lcnc 1 100
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
fault0.state
@expect hv0.sim_vel[1] ~ 0 0.5
@expect hv0.sim_f3_brake == 0
@expect hv0.sim_vel[2] ~ 62.8 2%
@expect fault0.state == 1
